     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Bogdan,<div><br></div><div>Sorry for the delay and thanks for your patience.</div><div><br></div><div>The correct answer, based on your plots, should be numClusters=1.  The most important indication would be that the HET and NLOH segments in the same log ratios in chr4. Whereas in the numClusters=2, chr4, the HET and clonal NLOH have different log ratios.  </div><div>However, TitanCNA does estimate its parameters by considering all chromosomes so there could be some stronger evidence of sub clonal events in other chromosomes.  </div><div>It is very interesting that the S_Dbw are both so low that it picked the incorrect solution (assuming all other chromosomes also support 1 cluster). </div><div>This is why it is still very important to manually inspect the results, as you have been doing. </div><div><br></div><div>Hope this helps answer your question.</div><div>Best,</div><div>Gavin</div></div>"
    ],
    [
